cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Formal Verify Anything: bounded proof search for Lean 4 with kernel-audited acceptance"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shayaun
    family-names: Nejad
repository-code: "https://github.com/allsmog/Formal-Verify-Anything"
url: "https://github.com/allsmog/Formal-Verify-Anything"
abstract: >-
  Automated theorem proving for Lean 4 and Mathlib. An LLM proposer (through
  the Codex CLI) or a deterministic tactic policy suggests proof steps, Lean
  checks every step, and a proof is accepted only after two fresh
  compilations and a kernel dependency audit. Includes miniF2F benchmarks
  with complete search traces and an atomic-token security model.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - automated theorem proving
  - neural theorem proving
  - formal verification
  - proof search
  - large language models
  - miniF2F
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-25"
